[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 2"""
 date="2026-09-24T14:23:45Z"
 content="""
A use case for this is having a directory special remote that is --sameas a
rsync special remote. `git-annex import --fast` from the directory special
remote imports the tree and that avoids needing to import from the rsync
special remote, which would be much slower for a large data set.

A second import step would be acceptable in this situation. 
The user would need to make sure that the files on the remotes
are unchanged from the directory import when running the rsync import.
This seems like it could be handled as a special flag to `git-annex import`.
"""]]
